<title>ITALY: Italy's Florence sees May CPI at +0.4 mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Florence sees May CPI at +0.4 mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>FLORENCE, Italy 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Florence said its May consumer price index stood at +0.4 percent month-on-month and +1.5 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In April, Florence's inflation rate was 0.0 and 1.5 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Florence is one of 11 Italian cities to have published inflation data Tuesday and Wednsday. The city's CPI weighs 6.08 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.</p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to April 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.4    (0.0)    1.5    (1.5)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.3    (0.1)   -0.5    (0.0)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	  -0.2    (0.2)   +1.8    (2.2)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges  -0.1    (0.4)    3.5    (5.1)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   1.0    (0.1)    2.4    (2.0)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.0    (0.0)    2.0    (2.1)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.2    (0.6)    1.0    (0.9)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.1   (-2.0)   -1.3   (-2.3)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0    (0.0)    4.5    (4.8)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.7    (0.0)    3.5    (3.3)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 1.6    (0.1)    2.9    (1.7)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
</text>
